.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis
.Nd post-quantum signatures, KEMs and sealed capsules of files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar args
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl V | Fl -version
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
records the exact files a result came from, signs that record with a
post-quantum signature (ML-DSA, FIPS 204, or SLH-DSA, FIPS 205) and checks
such records later.
It also signs and verifies single files, runs the ML-KEM (FIPS 203) and
HQC key encapsulation mechanisms, and prints and checks file digests.
It is a thin tool over the public C interface of
.Xr noqtis 3
and calls nothing else.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "version"
.It Cm keygen
Make a key pair.
See
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 .
.It Cm sign
Sign a file.
See
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 .
.It Cm verify
Check a signature.
See
.Xr noqtis-verify 1 .
.It Cm enc
Encapsulate a shared secret to a KEM public key.
See
.Xr noqtis-enc 1 .
.It Cm dec
Decapsulate a shared secret with a KEM secret key.
See
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 .
.It Cm hash
Print or check file digests in the format of
.Xr sha256sum 1 .
See
.Xr noqtis-hash 1 .
.It Cm seal
Seal a folder: write
.Pa noqtis.json
and
.Pa noqtis.sig
into it.
See
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 .
.It Cm check
Check a sealed folder against its seal.
See
.Xr noqtis-check 1 .
.It Cm prove
Prove that some files are in a format 2 capsule, without the others.
See
.Xr noqtis-prove 1 .
.It Cm rotate , revoke
Say that a seal key was replaced, or must no longer be trusted, for
.Cm check Fl -keys .
See
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1
and
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 .
.It Cm timestamp
Add an RFC 3161 timestamp to a folder sealed before.
See
.Xr noqtis-timestamp 1 .
.It Cm inspect
Show what a sealed folder says (format, algorithm, key fingerprint,
created, files, size, timestamp, meta) without checking it.
See
.Xr noqtis-inspect 1 .
.It Cm algs
List every algorithm and its sizes.
See
.Xr noqtis-algs 1 .
.It Cm version
Print the version.
See
.Xr noqtis-version 1 .
.It Cm help Op Ar command
Print the list of commands, or the options of one command.
.El
.Pp
Options follow the command.
A short option takes its value as the next argument or joined to it
.Pq Fl k Ns Ar key ;
a long option takes it as the next argument or after
.Ql =
.Pq Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key .
.Fl h
or
.Fl -help
after any command prints its usage.
.Fl -
ends the options; an argument
.Ql -
alone is a positional argument (standard input where a command allows it).
.Ss Algorithm names
Algorithms are named as
.Cm noqtis algs
prints them, without regard to case:
.Cm ML-DSA-44 , ML-DSA-65 , ML-DSA-87 ,
.Cm SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s , SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f , SLH-DSA-SHA2-192s ,
.Cm SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f , SLH-DSA-SHA2-256s , SLH-DSA-SHA2-256f ,
.Cm SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s , SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f , SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192s ,
.Cm SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192f , SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s , SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256f ,
.Cm ML-DSA-44+Ed25519 , ML-DSA-65+Ed25519 , ML-DSA-87+Ed25519
(post-quantum signatures, the last three hybrid),
.Cm Ed25519
(classical, not for seals) and
.Cm ML-KEM-512 , ML-KEM-768 , ML-KEM-1024 , HQC-128 , HQC-192 , HQC-256
(key encapsulation).
.Ss Key files
A key file is text: one header line, then the key bytes in the standard's
own encoding (FIPS 203, 204, 205; HQC v5.0.0) as base64 (RFC 4648, with
padding) in lines of 64 characters:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
noqtis-key-1 <algorithm> <pub|sec>
<base64>
\&...
.Ed
.Pp
Readers accept
.Ql \en
or
.Ql \er\en
line ends and reject any other character, non-canonical padding, a header
that is not exactly three space-separated fields, the wrong kind of key
.Po
.Ql pub
where a secret key is needed, or the reverse
.Pc ,
and a key whose decoded length is not the algorithm's size.
The base64 encoder and decoder run in constant time.
.Pp
Signatures and ciphertexts are raw bytes in the standard's encoding, with
no header.
A shared secret file holds the raw 32 bytes.
.Ss Secrets and files
Secret key and shared-secret files are created owner-only (mode 0600,
with
.Dv O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW
on POSIX; on Windows they inherit the folder's ACL) through unbuffered
streams.
No command overwrites an existing file unless given
.Fl -force ;
with it the old file is removed first, so the new one never inherits its
permissions or follows a link.
Every buffer that held a secret key, seed or shared secret is wiped before
it is freed.
No secret is printed: a shared secret reaches standard output only with
.Fl -stdout
(in hex), and keys never do.
.Pp
On Windows, arguments are read as UTF-16 and passed on as UTF-8, and
standard input and output are in binary mode.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
For every command:
.Bl -tag -width 3n
.It 0
Success: a signature is valid, every capsule check passed, every digest
matched.
.It 1
A verification failed: a bad or wrong-length signature, a failed capsule
check, a digest that differs or a listed file that is missing, a malformed
.Fl -check
line.
.It 2
A usage error, an unreadable or unwritable file, the wrong kind of key, or
a library error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Seal a folder, check it, change a file and check again:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me
ML-DSA-65 key pair: me (secret), me.pub (public)
$ noqtis seal -k me results
sealed results with ML-DSA-65
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results
\&...
results: OK (22 checks passed)
$ echo extra >> results/report.txt
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results; echo $?
\&...
FAIL  file                report.txt: size differs
\&...
results: FAILED (1 of 22 checks failed)
1
.Ed
